\f1\b \cf0 Poor Handling of Missing Data
\f0\b0 \
MLPs require imputation (e.g., mean/median), which 
\f1\b distorts clinical patterns
\f0\b0 .\
Missing lactate values imputed as "normal" \uc0\u8594  false negatives for sepsis.\

\f1\b Categorical Features
\f0\b0 \
Requires one-hot encoding (e.g., ICD-10 codes \uc0\u8594  70k columns).\
Unwieldy for real-world ED data.\

\f1\b Black-Box Interpretability
\f0\b0 \
No native feature importance \uc0\u8594  
\f1\b clinicians distrust predictions
\f0\b0 .\
"Why did the model suggest ICU transfer?"\

\f1\b Hyperparameter Sensitivity
\f0\b0 \
Needs careful tuning for stability.\
Learning rate/layer size changes \uc0\u8594  variance.\

\f1\b Performance on Tabular Data
\f0\b0 \
Outperformed by gradient boosting on structured EHR data.\
AUC 0.82 (MLP) vs. 
\f1\b 0.87 (CatBoost)
\f0\b0  for LoS > 6h.\

\f1\b Training Data Inefficiency
\f0\b0 \
Requires large datasets to avoid overfitting.\
EDs often have 
\f1\b <10k labeled examples
\f0\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

