\f1\b \cf0 Native Missing Data Handling
\f0\b0 \
Uses 
\f1\b surrogate splits
\f0\b0  (e.g., if lactate missing, uses HR + BP).\
No imputation needed.\

\f1\b Categorical Support
\f0\b0 \
Encodes ICD-10/SNOMED 
\f1\b without one-hot explosion
\f0\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 cat_features=["diagnosis_code", "triage"]
\f0\fs24 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Interpretability
\f0\b0 \

\f1\b SHAP values
\f0\b0  explain predictions (e.g., "\uc0\u11014 \u65039  HR + \u11015 \u65039  SBP drove ICU alert").\
Critical for clinician buy-in.\

\f1\b Robustness to Noise
\f0\b0 \
Ordered boosting reduces overfitting on small datasets.\
Ideal for EDs with 
\f1\b <10k patients/year
\f0\b0 .\

\f1\b Faster Training
\f0\b0 \
Converges in 
\f1\b <100 iterations
\f0\b0  on ED data.\
MLP requires epochs of tuning.\

\f1\b Calibration
\f0\b0 \
Isotonic regression \uc0\u8594  
\f1\b reliable risk scores
\f0\b0 .\
MLP often overconfident.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

